    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5810A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to authorizing\nthe dormitory authority to finance certain facilities for the Reece\nschool\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\nTo enable the Reece School to obtain funding and enter into contracts\nthrough the dormitory authority for the acquisition, financing,\nrefinancing, design construction, improvement, renovation, equipping,\nfurnishing or otherwise providing for facilities of the school.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 2 of section 1676 of the\npublic authorities law by adding a new undesignated subparagraph\nincluding the Reece School in the list of entities deemed to be a\n\"dormitory\".\n\nSection 2 amends subdivision I of section 1680 of the public\nauthorities law by adding a new undesignated paragraph including the\nReece School in the list of entities deemed to be an \"educational\ninstitution\".\n\nSection 3 provides that any contracts entered into by the dormitory\nauthority pursuant to this act shall be deemed state contracts.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nThe Reece School is one of the oldest non-profit special education\nelementary schools in New York City. It was founded in 1948 by Ellen\nS.  Reece and 'was originally housed in the home she once owned. Today\nthe Reece School is in a modern building, Located at 25 East 104th\nStreet.\n\nThe Reece School has a highly academic elementary special education\nprogram for 90 students, ages S to 13, who are psychologically fragile\nand may have learning or emotional disabilities or speech and language\nimpairments. The school's program is full day and is offered within a\nnurturing environment that is designed to provide high levels of\nacademic and emotional support. Children study a standard New York\nState Curriculum for grades K-6 in all academic areas, modified and\nsequenced to meet their individual needs as expressed in their\nIndividual Education Plan (IEP.)\n\nThis legislation will authorize the Dormitory Authority of the State\nof New York (DASNY) to support the construction of additional academic\nand therapy facilities at the school. The Reece School now operates\nbeyond full capacity, and additional facilities are needed to\naccommodate the needs of students at the school, and to enable the\nschool to serve additional children with special needs.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nTo be determined.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
